### Scope::getType() usage

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.3.x/website/src/developing-extensions/scope.md

Demonstrates using Scope::getType() to obtain the type of an expression, such as the variable on which a method is called. The returned type is an implementation of PHPStan\Type\Type.

```php
// $methodCall is PhpParser\Node\Expr\MethodCall
// On which type was the method called?
$calledOnType = $scope->getType($methodCall->var);
```

--------------------------------

### Scope

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.3.x/website/src/developing-extensions/scope.md

The most interesting method is `Scope::getType(PhpParser\Node\Expr $expr): PHPStan\Type\Type`. It allows us to ask for types of expressions like this:

```php
// $methodCall is PhpParser\Node\Expr\MethodCall
// On which type was the method called?
$calledOnType = $scope->getType($methodCall->var);
```

--------------------------------

### Create union and intersection types with normalization

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.3.x/website/src/developing-extensions/type-system.md

When creating custom types, use TypeCombinator::union() and TypeCombinator::intersect() instead of directly instantiating UnionType and IntersectionType to trigger type normalization.

```php
$union = new UnionType([$a, $b, $c]);
$intersection = new IntersectionType([$a, $b, $c]);
```

```php
$union = TypeCombinator::union($a, $b, $c);
$intersection = TypeCombinator::intersect($a, $b, $c);
```

--------------------------------

### MethodCallCollector: Collect method call data

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.3.x/website/src/_posts/using-phpstan-to-extract-data-about-your-codebase.md

Collects method call data by visiting every MethodCall node. Uses $scope->getMethodReflection() to resolve the declaring class of the called method, so calls to inherited methods record the parent class. Returns null when the method name is not an identifier or the method reflection cannot be resolved.

```php
use PhpParser\Node;
use PhpParser\Node\Expr\MethodCall;
use PHPStan\Analyser\Scope;
use PHPStan\Collectors\Collector;

/**
 * @implements Collector<MethodCall, array{callingClass?: string, callingMethod: string, calledClass: string, calledMethod: string}>
 */
class MethodCallCollector implements Collector
{
    public function getNodeType(): string
    {
        return MethodCall::class;
    }

    public function processNode(Node $node, Scope $scope)
    {
        $methodName = $node->name;
        if (!$methodName instanceof Node\Identifier) {
            return null;
        }

        // Find the class that declares the called method
        $type = $scope->getType($node->var);
        $methodReflection = $scope->getMethodReflection($type, $methodName->name);
        if ($methodReflection === null) {
            return null;
        }

        $calledClass = $methodReflection->getDeclaringClass()->getName();

        // Find the calling context
        $callingClass = '';
        if ($scope->isInClass()) {
            $callingClass = $scope->getClassReflection()->getName();
        }

        return [
            'callingClass' => $callingClass,
            'callingMethod' => $scope->getFunction()?->getName(),
            'calledClass' => $calledClass,
            'calledMethod' => $methodName->name,
        ];
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Select method variant with ParametersAcceptorSelector

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.3.x/website/src/developing-extensions/reflection.md

Use this snippet to select the appropriate variant of a method reflection when you have a PhpParser\Node\Expr\MethodCall expression. It returns the variant that matches the given arguments, from which you can obtain the parameters and return type.

```php
$variant = PHPStan\Reflection\ParametersAcceptorSelector::selectFromArgs(
	$scope,
	$methodCall->getArgs(),
	$methodReflection->getVariants()
);
$parameters = $variant->getParameters();
$returnType = $variant->getReturnType();
```

