### Walk the AST with NodeWalker

Source: https://github.com/thephpleague/commonmark/blob/2.10/docs/2.x/customization/abstract-syntax-tree.md

Use the walker() method to obtain a NodeWalker instance for pre-order traversal that emits events when entering and leaving nodes.

```php
use League\CommonMark\Node\NodeWalker;

/** @var NodeWalker $walker */
$walker = $document->walker();
while ($event = $walker->next()) {
    echo 'Now ' . ($event->isEntering() ? 'entering' : 'leaving') . ' a ' . get_class($event->getNode()) . ' node' . "\n";
}
```

--------------------------------

### Create a custom event listener

Source: https://github.com/thephpleague/commonmark/blob/2.10/docs/2.x/customization/event-dispatcher.md

Implement a class that processes DocumentParsedEvent to modify link attributes based on the environment configuration.

```php
use League\CommonMark\Environment\EnvironmentInterface;
use League\CommonMark\Event\DocumentParsedEvent;
use League\CommonMark\Extension\CommonMark\Node\Inline\Link;

class ExternalLinkProcessor
{
    private $environment;

    public function __construct(EnvironmentInterface $environment)
    {
        $this->environment = $environment;
    }

    public function onDocumentParsed(DocumentParsedEvent $event): void
    {
        $document = $event->getDocument();
        $walker = $document->walker();
        while ($event = $walker->next()) {
            $node = $event->getNode();

            // Only stop at Link nodes when we first encounter them
            if (!($node instanceof Link) || !$event->isEntering()) {
                continue;
            }

            $url = $node->getUrl();
            if ($this->isUrlExternal($url)) {
                $node->data->append('attributes/class', 'external-link');
            }
        }
    }

    private function isUrlExternal(string $url): bool
    {
        // Only look at http and https URLs
        if (!preg_match('/^https?:\/\//', $url)) {
            return false;
        }

        $host = parse_url($url, PHP_URL_HOST);

        return $host != $this->environment->getConfiguration()->get('host');
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Manually add CommonMarkCoreExtension to an Environment

Source: https://github.com/thephpleague/commonmark/blob/2.10/docs/2.x/extensions/commonmark.md

Register the extension manually when creating a custom Environment instance to enable standard Markdown syntax.

```php
use League\CommonMark\Environment\Environment;
use League\CommonMark\Extension\CommonMark\CommonMarkCoreExtension;
use League\CommonMark\MarkdownConverter;

// Define your configuration, if needed
$config = [];

// Create a new Environment with the core extension
$environment = new Environment($config);
$environment->addExtension(new CommonMarkCoreExtension());

// Instantiate the converter engine and start converting some Markdown!
$converter = new MarkdownConverter($environment);
echo $converter->convert('# Hello World!');
```

--------------------------------

### Manually executing the parsing and rendering process

Source: https://github.com/thephpleague/commonmark/blob/2.10/docs/2.x/customization/overview.md

Demonstrates how to manually configure an Environment, parse Markdown into an AST, and render it to HTML instead of using the default MarkdownConverter.

```php
use League\CommonMark\Parser\MarkdownParser;
use League\CommonMark\Environment\Environment;
use League\CommonMark\Renderer\HtmlRenderer;

$environment = new Environment([
    'html_input' => 'strip',
]);
$environment->addExtension(new CommonMarkCoreExtension());

$parser = new MarkdownParser($environment);
$htmlRenderer = new HtmlRenderer($environment);

$markdown = '# Hello World!';

$document = $parser->parse($markdown);
echo $htmlRenderer->renderDocument($document);

// <h1>Hello World!</h1>
```

--------------------------------

### CommonMark Core Extension

Source: https://github.com/thephpleague/commonmark/blob/2.10/docs/2.x/extensions/commonmark.md

The CommonMarkCoreExtension class provides the foundational Markdown syntax, including support for headers, code blocks, links, and images.

